#: src/podman-build.md:1
msgid "Building Redox"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:3
msgid ""
"Congrats on making it this far! Now you will build Redox. This process is "
"mainly for creating images targeting **x86-64** machines (Intel/AMD). The "
"process is similar when targeting i586, [ARM64](./aarch64.md) and RISC-V."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:5
msgid ""
"Redox build system is using **Rootless Podman**. **Podman** is used to avoid "
"bugs from different build environments (operating systems). You can find out "
"more about Podman on the [Official Podman documentation](https://docs.podman."
"io/en/latest/Introduction.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:7
msgid "Podman Build Overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:9
msgid ""
"**Podman** is a **container manager** that creates **containers** to execute "
"a Linux distribution **image**. In our case, we are creating an **Debian** "
"image, with a **Rust** installation and all the dependencies needed to build "
"the system and programs."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:11
msgid "New Working Directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:13
msgid ""
"📝 **Note:** If you have cloned our official repository, go to [Existing "
"Working Directory](#existing-working-directory)."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:15
msgid ""
"Open a terminal and ensure you have the `curl` program installed. You can "
"use `apt`, `dnf` or `apk` depending on your operating system."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:21
msgid ""
"Create a new directory and run `podman_bootstrap.sh` inside of it. This will "
"clone the repository, install **Podman** and extra software such as "
"**Rust**, **Git** and **QEMU**. It's a good practice to check the content of "
"[the script](https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/redox/raw/master/"
"podman_bootstrap.sh) before launching it."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:35
msgid ""
"The installation may take about 15 minutes on good network condition. You "
"may be asked for some question and sudo prompt along the installation."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:37
msgid "Update your path to include `cargo` and the Rust compiler."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:43
msgid "Navigate to the `redox` directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:49
msgid ""
"Create a configuration file and take a moment to read our [Build "
"Configuration Settings](./configuration-settings.md). The build "
"configuration is written to `.config`, and we recommend to start with "
"`REPO_BINARY=1` to speed up image build by downloading prebuilt programs "
"instead of compiling them."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:56 src/podman-build.md:94
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:59
msgid ""
"Build the system. The time needed in the first execution depends on "
"computer, system, and network performance/condition."
msgstr ""

