msgid ""
"You can immediately run the new image (`build/x86_64/desktop/harddrive.img`) "
"in a virtual machine with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:111
msgid ""
"The emulator will display the Redox GUI (Orbital). See [Using the emulation]"
"(./running-vm.md#using-the-emulation) for general instructions and [Trying "
"out Redox](./trying-out-redox.md) for things to try."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:113
msgid "Run without a GUI"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:115
msgid "To run the virtual machine without a GUI, use:"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:121
msgid ""
"If you want to capture the terminal output, read the [Debug Methods](./"
"troubleshooting.md#debug-methods) section."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:123
msgid ""
"💡 **Tip:** if you encounter problems running the virtual machine, try "
"turning off various virtualization features with `make qemu kvm=no` or `make "
"qemu iommu=no`. These same arguments can also be used with `build.sh`."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:125
msgid "QEMU Tap For Network Testing"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:127
msgid ""
"Expose Redox to other computers in the same local network. Configure QEMU "
"with a \"TAP\" which will allow other computers to test Redox client/server/"
"networking capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:129
msgid ""
"Please join the [chat](./chat.md) if this is something you are interested in "
"pursuing."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:131
msgid "Using build.sh script"
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:133
msgid ""
"`build.sh` is a shell script for quickly invoking `make` for a specified "
"variant, CPU architecture, and output file. It is created for quick one-off "
"commands to build everything without changing settings from `.config` file."
msgstr ""

#: src/podman-build.md:135
msgid ""
"💡 **Tip:** for doing Redox development, such settings should usually be "
"configured in the `.config` file (see the [Configuration Settings](./"
"configuration-settings.md) page). But for users who are just trying things "
"out, the `build.sh` script can be used to run `make` for you."
msgstr ""

